ch hope to begin with. [3360] \"It's no wonder that Yuki is the daughter of Yuki! She thinks about taking meaning from the overall composition. Your mother also often puts 'not in line' in her mouth... Oh, Yuki, I have a question for you. If I offend you, please forgive me.\" [3361] Jingma made a preamble before asking the question that had been bothering him since yesterday: \"Your left eye is not an artificial eye, right?\"\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 6:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:46:48 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nIt is said that the shoes are for entering the sacred garden and the small shrine, and each person is responsible for cleaning them, so no one else's shoes can be used. Ushio was scolded when he was a child for wearing his father's shoes. [902] Starting from the corridor, they pass through a small gate, and the paved stones extend towards the garden. Koi carp make splashing sounds in the pond, and everyone walks along the pond towards the small shrine. Although the distance is not far, this path is secluded from the main house and the annex by a bamboo wall that is one person high, so it is very quiet. There are no lights outside, so it must be very dark at night. Has Chikako never felt any fear since she started walking this path to the small shrine and staying there alone since she turned ten? [903] Oyuki left Ushio outside and opened the sliding door of the entrance. Inside is a small three and a half-tatami room and a small wooden sandal rack. Beyond the sliding door is Chikako's room, which is about ten tatami mats in size. On the opposite side are a closet and a sliding door, behind which there seems to be a four and a half-tatami room and a washroom. Although an air conditioner is installed, there is no bathroom. Just looking at the layout of the house, it would have a cheap student apartment feel. [904] The current Hikone-no-dono, Chik