ar. [914] \"I see, because you're a god, you can't do anything openly in the main house.\" [915] Jingma took Yuying for a university friend and agreed with her words, only to realize that she was a seventeen-year-old girl and hastily stopped talking. Yuying chuckled and pointed to the desk. [916] \"It's said that an envelope with Jingma's name is placed on this table, and it's placed seriously in the center.\" [917] That letter had already been taken by the police. [918] \"I guess I was cursed, that letter made me look like a murderer.\" [919] \"Even without that letter, you would have been suspected, because Jingma, you are very suspicious. A man, staying in a remote hot spring resort, someone who is either planning to commit suicide or commit a crime.\" [920] Jingma's body stiffened suddenly. However, Yuying seemed not to care about Jingma's personal matters. [921] \"Moreover, being cursed by someone you don't know in an unknown situation, such things happen in the world. If you worry about every little thing, you won't be able to talk to people outside. This kind of behavior is like being suspicious every time you sneeze that someone is saying something bad about you.\" [922] Yuki spoke in a straightforward manner and began to check the interior of the room, a very unique way. She stood with her hands on her hips in the center of the room, slowly moving her gaze like a spotlight in all directions. After scanning the room, she began to search through drawers, closets, and wardrobes one by one. [923] \"It's so strange, I hardly see it in TV dramas.\" [924] \"First, grasp the overall situation, and then distinguish each part and check it. If you start with the details, you won't see the grand contradictions. This method is also convenient when looking for things, so Jingma, pay attention and learn from it.\" [925] After lecturing with her index finger raised, Yuki rolled up her sleeves and headed towards the small room on the inside. The small room had no windows and only a door leading to the bathroom. Along the walls were long, narrow bookshelves filled with ancient books and a large rectangular box with a lid, which was almost like a storage room. Inside the box were clothes reminiscent of a female official from the Heian period, as well as Spring Vegetable's clothes when she was young, a backpack, and toys. According to Ando, all of Spring Vegetable's belongings were kept here, not in the main house. Originally, when she inherited the position of Yashiro, her belongings would have been directly moved to the shrine, so she would never have to keep them in the main house. However, the scheduled relocation in a few days seemed to force her to return to her \"home.\" [926] \"Did you find anything?\" [927] After the investigation was completed, Oyama left the room and Shouma asked her. Perhaps because of the wind, his cheeks were flushed. [928] Oyama shook her head wearily: \"I already knew, it's no good. The initial search is very important. The police picked through it, and it seems that nothing important was left... However, there's one thing I'm particularly concerned about. A letter addressed to Shouma, which was supposedly written with a very thick red marker pen, but I didn't see any in the room, and Mr. Bessho didn't say he confiscated any pens either, Shouma, do you know?\" [929] \"Red marker pen? Maybe Sumi and the others know something... However, with all that's happened, I don't think they would discard or take Shion's things without permission.\" [930] Shouma was puzzled, but still gave a negative answer. [931] \"Then maybe the murderer took it. Jingma, be happy.\" [932] She suddenly threw out this sentence. [933] \"Why?\" Jingma asked. [934] \"The marker pen is the murderer's, or perhaps he accidentally put it in his own pocket. In either case, there is the following possibility: the murderer was with Spring's girl and made her write your name; or he imitated her handwriting and wrote your name by hand.\" [935] \