n't come here anymore. And she wasn't like Spring Vegetable who came here every day, only visiting once or twice a month.\" [952] \"So, it's more accurate to say that Spring Vegetable girl likes to look at the scenery here rather than for duty or mission?\" [953] Uesugi's expression clouded over. \"Spring Vegetable has never left this village. Although she wasn't prohibited, her grandfather wouldn't give her a good look either. Of course, you can't see outside the village from here.\" [954] From the time of her birth until now, fifteen years have passed, and the scenery Spring Vegetable has seen from here is her entire world. If she were still alive, she would have continued to do so in the future. [955]\n[956] \"It would be better if she never knew the outside world.\" [957] Oyama murmured softly, letting the wind blow through her hair and skirt, and looked around for a moment. [958] \"You can't see the mansion or the garden from the balcony, it's blocked by the tower. Conversely, you can't see the balcony from the mansion. In other words, the murderer can look at the dragon's head without worrying about being questioned by the people in the mansion. I found it strange that, even in the early morning, no matter how early, one could be seen by the people in the mansion just by being careless, yet they would take the risk to come to the balcony to check the condition of the dragon's head. However, it is also possible to be questioned when entering or leaving this tower, and the murderer's obsession with the dragon's head is beyond doubt... Have you thought of anything, Hige?\" [959] Hige shook his head apologetically:\n[960] \"I only heard a little about the dragon's head when I was a child... and I'm not very interested in it.\" [961] \"But there must be some reason for the threatening letter, right? Perhaps it's necessary to investigate the legend more thoroughly.\" [962] \"But isn't it strange?\" Shizuma countered, picking up on something he couldn't shake off in 