he murderer.\" [980] \"Just so you know, I'm not the murderer... Ah, Hoshibe-san, Mr. Chou is looking for you.\" [981] \"Really?\" [982] Gen looked back at Iwakura with a deep look of doubt. [983] Iwakura exaggeratedly shrugged his shoulders and said: \"Ah, I'm not lying. Because I don't want you to hate me more.\" [984] Probably because he thought he wasn't lying, Gen reluctantly turned back, but he still reluctantly went back. [985] \"So, you're not the killer?\" [986] With her fan closed in her hand, Oyuki rhythmically tapped it and looked at Gen with her emotionless left eye, just like her artificial right eye. [987] \"I think so, but many people don't agree. What do you think, Detective Miss?\" [988] Rocking his shoulders lightly, Gen deftly avoided the question. He was an impeccable man. [989] \"I'm skeptical. However, it seems that you're completely unfazed even when suspected, which gives off a sense of security. You must believe that you won't be implicated in the end.\" [990] \"Do I look like someone who is happy about committing the perfect crime? You're overestimating me. Being suspected without panic...well, that's just my personality, and I've suffered for it, but I haven't changed.\" [991] Inagawa chuckled bitterly, revealing his white teeth. [992] \"I see. Can we talk a bit?\" [993] \"Sure. I'm eating for free here anyway, so I have plenty of time. Standing around talking is a bit inappropriate, so let's sit over there. I'm sort of on a 'vacation' after all.\" [994] He pointed to the white bench in front of the door. He sat down first, and Oyim sat down beside him. Since it was a two-person bench, there was no room for Shizuma. However, both of them ignored the assistant's presence and continued to converse. [995] \"You said you're on a 'vacation,' so you have another purpose, right?\" [996] \"It's true that my body is worn out, but they brought me here because they wanted me to inherit the family tradition. I'm a distant relative of the Uzuki family